# Both functions have a guard, and a slow body for what it turns away; neither slow body holds a Builtin operation. That of plain() is written straight.
# That of letsGo() holds a ReleaseHint, at `list = null`. Straight code keeps each value in a word of the frame and does not know which read of it is the last, so it has no form for the hint:
# the body is walked, and the list is let go while the function still runs.
